<article class="env-lemma" id="09YF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09YF">Lemma <span data-tag="09YF">5.15.8</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $T \subset X$ be a subset. Suppose </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$T$ is retrocompact in $X$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
quasi-compact opens form a basis for the topology on $X$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then for a constructible set $E \subset X$ the intersection $E \cap T$ is constructible in $T$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose that $V \subset X$ is retrocompact open in $X$. It suffices to show that $V \cap T$ is retrocompact in $T$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/005I" data-tag="005I">5.15.3</a>. To show this let $W \subset T$ be open and quasi-compact. By assumption (2) we can find a quasi-compact open $W' \subset X$ such that $W = T \cap W'$ (details omitted). Hence $V \cap T \cap W = V \cap T \cap W'$ is the intersection of $T$ with the quasi-compact open $V \cap W'$ as $V$ is retrocompact in $X$. Thus $V \cap T \cap W$ is quasi-compact. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>